---
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";

/*
 * Etap 1.12, before registration opens: the operator is named here only as
 * akApp Studio. Under an unregistered business (NDG) the service provider is
 * a natural person, so add the full name and address to section 1, and the
 * same in privacy.astro.
 */
const TOC = [
  { id: "who", label: "1. Who runs Xebeka" },
  { id: "beta", label: "2. A game still being built" },
  { id: "needs", label: "3. What you need" },
  { id: "account", label: "4. Your account" },
  { id: "characters", label: "5. Characters" },
  { id: "rules", label: "6. Rules of play" },
  { id: "breaches", label: "7. When the rules are broken" },
  { id: "price", label: "8. Price" },
  { id: "content", label: "9. The game and its content" },
  { id: "responsibility", label: "10. Our responsibility" },
  { id: "complaints", label: "11. Complaints" },
  { id: "changes", label: "12. Changes to these terms" },
  { id: "law", label: "13. Law" },
];
---
<Doc
  title="Terms of Service · Xebeka"
  description="The terms of Xebeka, the online RPG played in the browser, including the rules of play."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  updated="27 September 2026"
  toc={TOC}
>
  <p>
    These terms apply to Xebeka, the online role-playing game at xebeka.com, and to your account
    in it. By creating an account you agree to them, so please read them first. They include the
    rules of play, which keep the game fair for everyone. How we handle your data is described in
    the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">1. Who runs Xebeka</h2>
  <p>
    Xebeka is run by <a href="https://akappstudio.pl">akApp Studio</a>. You can reach us at
    <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a>, the address for everything these
    terms mention: questions, reports and complaints.
  </p>

  <h2 id="beta">2. A game still being built</h2>
  <p>
    Xebeka is in beta. Creatures, items, maps and balance change as the game grows, and the game
    may be unavailable for a while when it is updated. During the beta, characters and their
    progress may be reset, in particular when the game moves to a new server. Whenever we can, we
    announce a reset on this site before it happens.
  </p>

  <h2 id="needs">3. What you need</h2>
  <p>
    A current web browser with JavaScript turned on, on a computer or a phone, and an internet
    connection. There is nothing to install.
  </p>

  <h2 id="account">4. Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You must be at least 13 years old to create an account. If you are under 18, read these terms
      together with a parent or guardian.
    </li>
    <li>
      You create an account with an email address and a password, or with a Google account. The
      agreement between us starts when you create it and lasts until it is deleted.
    </li>
    <li>Keep your password to yourself. You are responsible for what happens on your account.</li>
    <li>An account is personal. Do not sell it, share it or give it to someone else.</li>
    <li>
      You can delete your account at any time in Manage account. This removes the account and all
      its characters for good.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="characters">5. Characters</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An account holds up to five characters.</li>
    <li>
      A name is 3 to 20 letters (A to Z), in up to three words. It must not be offensive, pretend to
      be staff, or copy the name of a creature or of a character in the game. We may change or
      remove a name that breaks this rule.
    </li>
    <li>
      A character you delete is removed 7 days later. Until then you can change your mind and cancel
      the deletion.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rules">6. Rules of play</h2>
  <p>Xebeka is a shared world. These rules keep it fair:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Play yourself.</strong> No bots, macros or programs that play for you, no modified game
      files, and no tampering with the game's data or its connection.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Report bugs instead of using them.</strong> If you find a way to gain an advantage the
      game did not intend, tell us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Respect other players.</strong> No harassment, threats or hate speech, and no sharing
      anyone's personal information.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No scams.</strong> Do not trick other players out of their items or accounts.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>No real-money trading.</strong> Do not buy or sell characters, items or gold for real
      money.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Do not pretend to be staff.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Nothing unlawful.</strong> Do not post or send unlawful content through the game.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Fighting other players is part of the game from level 10 and does not by itself break these rules.</p>

  <h2 id="breaches">7. When the rules are broken</h2>
  <p>
    We may warn you, suspend your account for a time, or delete it, depending on how serious the
    breach is and whether it is repeated. If you think we got it wrong, write to us and we will look
    at it again.
  </p>

  <h2 id="price">8. Price</h2>
  <p>
    Xebeka is free to play. If optional paid features are added later, their price and terms will
    be shown before you can buy them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="content">9. The game and its content</h2>
  <p>
    The game, its code and its art belong to us or to the artists who licensed their work (see
    <a href="/credits/">Credits</a>). You get a personal right to play. Characters and items exist
    only inside the game and are not your property.
  </p>

  <h2 id="responsibility">10. Our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep Xebeka running and your progress safe, but during the beta we cannot promise that
    the game will always be available, that it is free of errors, or that progress will never be lost
    or reset. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, or
    takes away your rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaints">11. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If something does not work as it should, write to
    <a href="mailto:kontakt@xebeka.com">kontakt@xebeka.com</a> with the email address of your account
    and a description of the problem. We answer within 14 days.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may change these terms as the game develops, for example when new features arrive, and we
    announce significant changes on this site before they take effect. If you do not agree with a
    change, you can delete your account. If you keep playing after it takes effect, the new terms
    apply to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="law">13. Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by Polish law. If you play as a consumer, you also keep the protection
    that the law of the country where you live gives you.
  </p>
</Doc>
